{#-
  Issue 1102 — the Rust entry TU, as a shape you can read.

  This is the `nros codegen entry --lang rust` output. It mirrors the
  `nros::main!()` proc-macro's `OwnedSpin` branch, which stays the canonical
  compile-time emitter; this form exists so the two can be byte-diffed
  (issue 0302).

  Every value below arrives ALREADY CORRECT from Rust: `board_path` is
  resolved through `nros_orchestration_ir`, and every literal in `params`,
  `remaps`, `qos_overrides`, `identity` and `depfiles` is already escaped by
  `lit_str` / `quote_str`. This template chooses where a literal goes, never
  how to quote one — quoting is a correctness property and a template that got
  it wrong would fail silently.

  ## `links_std` — the one place this template may name `std`

  Issue 1409, which is issue 1381 in this producer. The hosted `fn main()`
  below is the only `std`-naming text here, and it is emitted only when
  `links_std` is true. That flag is
  `nros_orchestration_ir::board_entry_links_std(board)`, the same fact
  `nros::main!`'s `hosted_std_scaffold_ts` is gated on.

  A `#[cfg]` cannot answer this and this one used to try. `#[cfg(not(target_os
  = "none"))]` asks "is the TARGET hosted"; the question is "does this CRATE
  have `std`", and `#![no_std]` is orthogonal to the target OS. The SAME tool
  writes `#![no_std]` at the top of a `board-run` / `zephyr-staticlib` entry TU
  (`builder/entry.rs`), and such a crate built with no `--target` compiles for
  the HOST, takes the hosted arm, and still has no `std` in its crate root.
  Measured: that TU, host triple, `error[E0433]: cannot find std in the crate
  root`, twice.

  The cfg STAYS on what is emitted, because a hosted-main board (native,
  `threadx-linux`) is still built for more than one OS — and it is the
  proc-macro's wider spelling now. The narrow one also let NuttX through, and
  NuttX has been `#![no_std]` since phase-359 W7; the `target_os = "nuttx"`
  C-ABI `main` below is the arm the proc-macro emits for it and this template
  did not have.

  There is no `core`/`alloc` spelling for an exit status: the fix is not to
  spell it differently but not to emit it. An entry that cannot link libstd has
  no process to exit.

  Whitespace is load-bearing: this output is byte-compared against
  `testdata/rust_native_one.rs`.
-#}
// Generated by `nros codegen entry --lang rust`
//   bringup = {{ bringup }}
//   launch  = {{ launch }}
//   board   = {{ board }}
//
// DO NOT EDIT — re-run `cargo build` to regenerate. The Rust
// `nros::main!()` proc-macro is the canonical compile-time
// emitter; this CLI-baked form mirrors its `OwnedSpin` branch.

{% for d in depfiles %}const _: &[u8] = ::core::include_bytes!({{ d }});
{% endfor %}
fn __nros_entry_run() -> ::core::result::Result<
    (),
    ::nros::__macro_support::nros_platform::RuntimeError,
> {
    <{{ board_path }} as ::nros::__macro_support::nros_platform::BoardEntry>::run(
        |runtime: &mut ::nros::__macro_support::nros_platform::RuntimeCtx<'_>|
            -> ::core::result::Result<
                (),
                ::nros::__macro_support::nros_platform::RuntimeError,
            >
    {
{%- for n in nodes %}
            runtime.params = &[{{ n.params }}];
            runtime.remaps = &[{{ n.remaps }}];
            runtime.qos_overrides = &[{{ n.qos_overrides }}];
            runtime.node_identity = {{ n.identity }};
            ::{{ n.pkg }}::register(runtime)?;
{%- endfor %}
            ::core::result::Result::Ok(())
        },
    )
}

{% if links_std %}
#[cfg(not(any(target_os = "none", target_os = "nuttx")))]
fn main() {
    if let ::core::result::Result::Err(e) = __nros_entry_run() {
        ::std::eprintln!("{}: {}", ::core::env!("CARGO_PKG_NAME"), e);
        ::std::process::exit(1);
    }
}
{% endif %}
#[cfg(target_os = "nuttx")]
#[unsafe(no_mangle)]
pub extern "C" fn main(
    _argc: i32,
    _argv: *const *const ::core::ffi::c_char,
) -> i32 {
    match __nros_entry_run() {
        ::core::result::Result::Ok(()) => 0,
        ::core::result::Result::Err(_) => 1,
    }
}

#[cfg(target_os = "none")]
#[unsafe(no_mangle)]
pub extern "C" fn main() -> i32 {
    match __nros_entry_run() {
        ::core::result::Result::Ok(()) => 0,
        ::core::result::Result::Err(_) => 1,
    }
}
